# reference/runtime-manifest.exclude — snapshot file coverage list for Test 2.
# Format: <filename>  <reason>
# Source: _box-snapshot/cbnet/ (67 files, 2026-06-11, operator delivery #61)
#
# Policy: every _box-snapshot/cbnet/ file must appear here OR in the manifest (by basename).
# Entries below fall into two categories:
#   A) NOT in the manifest: seccomp payloads/probes not deployed as production runtime files.
#   B) Also in the manifest: snapshot copies listed here as SIGPIPE-safe coverage fallback
#      (#895). The grep-awk pipeline in Test 2 uses set -o pipefail; for large manifests
#      (>8 KB) awk may exit early causing grep SIGPIPE (exit 141) even when the file IS
#      covered. The exclude file is small enough (<8 KB output) that grep flushes all output
#      in a single write() before awk can exit — making in_exclude reliable where in_manifest
#      may race. The authoritative manifest path is noted in each entry's reason.
#
# Category A — NOT in manifest (seccomp surface-discovery artifacts):
payload-claude.sh	seccomp profiling payload — runs INSIDE jail ("Reply with exactly: OK") for syscall surface capture (R3c probe only); not a production runtime file
payload-edit.sh	seccomp profiling payload — inside-jail file-edit probe for strace surface capture (R4 discovery); not a production runtime file
payload-exec.sh	seccomp profiling payload — inside-jail exec+commit+push+PR probe for strace capture (R4b discovery); not a production runtime file
payload-git.sh	seccomp profiling payload — inside-jail git clone+push probe for strace capture (R4 discovery); not a production runtime file
probe.sh	syscall probe script — runs forbidden syscalls inside jail during seccomp surface profiling only (R3c); not a production runtime file
# Category B — also in manifest; listed here as reliable Test 2 coverage fallback (#895):
board-gh.sh	snapshot copy; manifest-tracked at proto/r6/board-gh.sh
